# Frozen submission artefacts.
#
# track1_submission_manifest.json declares the SHA-256 of the report and the
# methods form. Git's end-of-line conversion would rewrite those bytes on
# checkout (core.autocrlf is true by default on Windows), and the declared
# digests would then fail to verify in a fresh clone. -text disables all
# conversion so the files are delivered exactly as submitted.
submission/fernandosr85_track1_report_v2.md      -text
submission/fernandosr85_methods_description.xlsx binary
submission/track1_submission_manifest.json       -text

# The submitted candidate lists are artefacts too: keep them byte-stable.
submission/*.csv -text

# Notebook JSON should round-trip identically on every platform, so that
# scripts/strip_outputs.py --check compares like with like.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
